1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:01,710
[Disclaimer:
All depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:03,450
and for entertainment purposes only;
viewer discretion is advised]

3
00:00:12,090 --> 00:00:17,370
[Your Third Series]

4
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:18,560
Hey!

5
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:19,990
It's damn near impossible
to track you down,

6
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:20,780
Mr. Sarm.

7
00:00:25,010 --> 00:00:26,590
Quickly! Come on!

8
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:33,870
Hey!

9
00:00:34,790 --> 00:00:36,000
And where exactly are we going?

10
00:00:36,090 --> 00:00:37,180
To the boat, obviously.

11
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:38,500
Never heard of it?

12
00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:39,990
"The safest place

13
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:41,680
is often the most dangerous one."

14
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:46,060
Oh!

15
00:00:46,770 --> 00:00:47,890
Hey! Jam!

16
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:49,380
Jam!

17
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:54,020
Jam.

18
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,040
What are you going to do now?

19
00:00:56,210 --> 00:00:57,580
I'm going to stay here.

20
00:00:57,890 --> 00:00:58,760
Mr. Sarm!

21
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:33,780
You are still awake?

22
00:01:37,350 --> 00:01:38,900
The night is far from over.

23
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:40,300
By the way...

24
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:42,720
it's almost 2 A.M.

25
00:01:43,289 --> 00:01:44,430
Still not back in your body yet?

26
00:01:45,390 --> 00:01:46,710
I am not the Krasue.

27
00:01:46,990 --> 00:01:47,910
The Krasue.

28
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:51,840
Oh, the Krasue.

29
00:01:52,910 --> 00:01:53,860
The Krasue, huh?

30
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:57,690
The Krasue.

31
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:02,200
Are you...

32
00:02:02,390 --> 00:02:03,880
alright?

33
00:02:16,790 --> 00:02:18,190
Well, I'm officially heartbroken.

34
00:02:25,990 --> 00:02:26,990
I miss Ghibli.

35
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:28,890
Ghibli?

36
00:02:29,450 --> 00:02:31,240
Ghibli is a pygmy owl
that lives at the bungalow.

37
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:32,880
It loves coming to see me,

38
00:02:33,090 --> 00:02:34,900
always keeping me company at night.

39
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:36,640
I haven't seen it in days.

40
00:02:40,510 --> 00:02:40,950
Oh.

41
00:02:40,970 --> 00:02:43,100
Don't tell me to go back to
the bungalow or anything.

42
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:45,090
I refuse to go back to
either the bungalow or Pak Chong.

43
00:02:47,130 --> 00:02:48,500
How about...

44
00:02:48,690 --> 00:02:50,070
Is there anything you would like to share?

45
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:55,100
I'm trying to get over it.

46
00:02:58,990 --> 00:03:01,010
I've been goofing around for six months,

47
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:04,980
and I'm losing my mind.

48
00:03:07,330 --> 00:03:08,880
I only sleep two to three hours a night.

49
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:15,150
Are you really that heartbroken?

50
00:03:16,390 --> 00:03:17,390
Don't rub it in,

51
00:03:19,310 --> 00:03:20,750
or I'll cry right in front of you.

52
00:03:24,090 --> 00:03:26,060
If you want to get over it,

53
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:28,130
the first step is accepting the truth.

54
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,660
And how am I not accepting the truth?

55
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:31,660
Like this.

56
00:03:34,730 --> 00:03:35,579
Do you know

57
00:03:36,210 --> 00:03:38,690
what the last words I said to PiMai were?

58
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:44,510
"Hap-Pi New Year."

59
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:45,400
Huh?

60
00:03:48,090 --> 00:03:49,490
I told him...

61
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:51,180
I wouldn't make him feel uncomfortable.

62
00:03:51,790 --> 00:03:53,190
I'd only see him as a younger brother,

63
00:03:53,390 --> 00:03:55,180
and I wanted him to see me
as just an older brother.

64
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:02,480
Can I get a round of applause

65
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:03,890
worthy of a main character?

66
00:04:07,710 --> 00:04:08,400
Louder!

67
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:12,300
Louder.

68
00:04:15,230 --> 00:04:15,940
Enough.

69
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:20,079
Who taught you to be so extra?

70
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:31,090
So, Sib and PiMai

71
00:04:31,290 --> 00:04:32,390
are back together?

72
00:04:32,810 --> 00:04:34,860
Their relationship never really ended.

73
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:38,280
They just needed some time apart.

74
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:40,780
I just asked them, actually.

75
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:44,159
You have a knife?

76
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:45,770
Just stab me in the heart already.

77
00:04:46,550 --> 00:04:47,510
After six months apart,

78
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:49,000
they're already in heaven.

79
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:52,290
People deal with problems
differently, do they not?

80
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:57,290
Go ahead.

81
00:04:57,890 --> 00:04:58,420
Keep talking.

82
00:04:58,450 --> 00:04:59,370
I want to hear more.

83
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:03,110
Someday...

84
00:05:03,830 --> 00:05:06,190
you will find someone you love

85
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:08,090
who loves you back.

86
00:05:21,930 --> 00:05:23,120
That quote...

87
00:05:23,650 --> 00:05:24,870
It's exactly what PiMai said.

88
00:05:28,990 --> 00:05:30,510
I don't think that person exists.

89
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:35,310
But the boy named Lantao is kind of sweet...

90
00:05:35,340 --> 00:05:36,740
Stop it right there.

91
00:05:37,580 --> 00:05:38,450
Don't.

92
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:39,470
Don't say that.

93
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:42,500
Just let him have a bright future.

94
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:45,710
So you know that

95
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:48,170
being with you
would only lead to a bleak future.

96
00:05:48,210 --> 00:05:49,210
Jam!

97
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,960
Always taking a dig at me.

98
00:05:55,409 --> 00:05:56,909
Am I not meant for love?

99
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:00,280
Why did you ask me that?

100
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:01,820
You just said that

101
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:04,510
being with me
would only lead to a bleak future.

102
00:06:05,090 --> 00:06:07,020
I was just teasing.

103
00:06:07,410 --> 00:06:08,290
Teasing?

104
00:06:09,590 --> 00:06:11,110
Careful, I might just tease you back.

105
00:06:17,490 --> 00:06:19,390
If there's anything
you'd like to share with me,

106
00:06:20,490 --> 00:06:21,790
feel free, by the way.

107
00:06:23,890 --> 00:06:25,700
I don't like owing anyone anything.

108
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:30,600
Mr. Sarm...

109
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:37,400
Mr. Sarm.

110
00:06:45,190 --> 00:06:46,000
Please...

111
00:06:46,590 --> 00:06:49,290
get your act together soon.

112
00:06:58,810 --> 00:06:59,690
Ow!

113
00:07:00,410 --> 00:07:01,560
Whoa...

114
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:02,980
So heavy...

115
00:07:06,750 --> 00:07:07,870
Well then,

116
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:11,000
I guess you are sleeping here.

117
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:47,990
Someday,

118
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:50,270
you will find someone you love

119
00:07:50,610 --> 00:07:51,890
who loves you back.

120
00:07:59,010 --> 00:08:04,290
[Your Third Series]

121
00:08:14,790 --> 00:08:18,720
♫Still feeling lonely? Well, you've got me,♫

122
00:08:18,750 --> 00:08:23,190
♫Keeping you busy every day♫

123
00:08:23,900 --> 00:08:27,840
♫I might not be the one you wanted,♫

124
00:08:27,910 --> 00:08:32,610
♫But give it time, you'll love me anyway♫

125
00:08:33,059 --> 00:08:37,539
♫It's your heart, so it's your choice,♫

126
00:08:37,590 --> 00:08:42,030
♫I won't ever stand in your way♫

127
00:08:42,169 --> 00:08:46,430
♫But when they make you blue,♫

128
00:08:46,470 --> 00:08:50,120
♫Can you please let me take care of you?♫

129
00:08:51,150 --> 00:08:55,820
♫I'm here to love you as myself,
not as a surrogate♫

130
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:59,610
♫Let me be your safe space
when you need a break♫

131
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:04,630
♫Who cares if I'm not your first or second?♫

132
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:09,510
♫At least being your third still counts♫

133
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:14,130
♫I'm here to love you,
no matter who left you with heartache♫

134
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:17,840
♫Just let me heal your heart,
lending you my aid♫

135
00:09:17,870 --> 00:09:22,980
♫Have faith and believe in love once more♫

136
00:09:23,010 --> 00:09:24,990
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

137
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:28,220
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

138
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:31,580
[Your Third Series]

139
00:09:43,530 --> 00:09:45,800
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

140
00:09:46,390 --> 00:09:47,300
Ouch...

141
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:48,490
Ow...

142
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:28,240
Is he awake?

143
00:10:40,650 --> 00:10:43,210
Sib sent Snoop here just to suffer,

144
00:10:43,770 --> 00:10:45,600
and Snoop willingly took on the task.

145
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:49,010
That's why we've been on the run like this.

146
00:10:50,970 --> 00:10:53,520
I didn't mean to drag him along with me,

147
00:10:54,450 --> 00:10:56,340
but I can't just leave him out there.

148
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:58,890
Since we're in the same boat,

149
00:10:59,140 --> 00:11:01,110
we can't just go our separate ways.

150
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:03,810
At first,

151
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:06,530
my goal was to make myself
so insufferable that he'd leave.

152
00:11:06,810 --> 00:11:07,890
But honestly,

153
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:10,190
having Jam here...

154
00:11:10,330 --> 00:11:11,410
isn't that bad.

155
00:11:13,510 --> 00:11:14,610
It's actually the opposite.

156
00:11:14,650 --> 00:11:16,290
Jam is like positive energy with legs.

157
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,740
You are all bark and no bite.

158
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:19,900
But sometimes, he's so supportive that

159
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:22,330
I want to support his face with my fist.

160
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,620
Boiled crabs...

161
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:31,300
What's with him?

162
00:11:32,730 --> 00:11:34,400
Boiled crabs...

163
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,340
Boiled crabs...

164
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:43,930
I've been alive for 30 years,

165
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:46,840
and I've never seen anyone
talk about food in their sleep.

166
00:11:47,310 --> 00:11:48,510
That's the spirit,

167
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:49,850
I guess...

168
00:12:07,870 --> 00:12:09,590
Boiled crabs...

169
00:12:54,630 --> 00:12:56,050
Whoa...

170
00:12:57,610 --> 00:12:59,230
What can I get you, handsome?

171
00:12:59,260 --> 00:13:00,310
Uh...

172
00:13:00,660 --> 00:13:02,780
I'll have five kilos of crabs.

173
00:13:02,810 --> 00:13:03,810
Oh...

174
00:13:03,930 --> 00:13:05,020
Since you want the whole lot...

175
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:05,540
No problem.

176
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:06,930
I'll throw in some freebies:

177
00:13:06,970 --> 00:13:08,930
five kilos of shrimp
and five kilos of mantis shrimp, on the house.

178
00:13:09,110 --> 00:13:10,110
If you don't mind, Uncle.

179
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:11,710
Whoa, you're awesome.

180
00:13:12,310 --> 00:13:13,890
They are for sale.

181
00:13:14,220 --> 00:13:15,180
You might as well

182
00:13:15,220 --> 00:13:16,310
just give them all away.

183
00:13:18,730 --> 00:13:19,330
Then

184
00:13:19,410 --> 00:13:20,520
I'll buy it all.

185
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:21,360
I'll take everything.

186
00:13:21,410 --> 00:13:23,300
This handsome fellow will pay for it.

187
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:25,610
As for your trouble with her,

188
00:13:25,810 --> 00:13:27,010
you're on your own, Uncle.

189
00:13:33,710 --> 00:13:34,710
Why are you staring at me?

190
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,110
Or...

191
00:13:39,410 --> 00:13:40,290
am I that handsome?

192
00:13:41,610 --> 00:13:42,520
Young man,

193
00:13:42,590 --> 00:13:44,290
let me take a closer look at you.

194
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:45,420
Of course.

195
00:13:50,110 --> 00:13:52,310
Are you the same person?

196
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,320
Same person as who?

197
00:13:56,130 --> 00:13:57,230
Oh!

198
00:13:57,260 --> 00:13:59,210
The guy from the soap opera last night.

199
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:00,600
But you, young man,

200
00:14:00,630 --> 00:14:01,640
are much more handsome.

201
00:14:01,660 --> 00:14:03,130
I knew it!

202
00:14:03,850 --> 00:14:05,250
Whatever you've got,

203
00:14:05,330 --> 00:14:06,410
I'll take it all!

204
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:08,050
- Okay. Sure thing.
- I'll take it all.

205
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:09,100
I'll take the ice, too.

206
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:10,060
No problem.

207
00:14:10,270 --> 00:14:12,390
We'll even cook them
and deliver them to you.

208
00:14:12,430 --> 00:14:13,820
Whoa...

209
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:14,660
Where are you staying?

210
00:14:14,690 --> 00:14:16,190
Oh, my resort is...

211
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:17,320
There. Over there.

212
00:14:17,350 --> 00:14:18,320
It's nearby.

213
00:14:18,810 --> 00:14:19,810
Oh.

214
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:21,610
You're both good-looking and kind-hearted.

215
00:14:23,250 --> 00:14:24,030
All good?

216
00:14:24,060 --> 00:14:25,330
- Yes.
- Thank you.

217
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:26,520
Alright.

218
00:14:40,210 --> 00:14:40,990
Hey.

219
00:14:41,230 --> 00:14:42,250
Who was that just now?

220
00:14:43,310 --> 00:14:44,310
Oh.

221
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:48,550
Just a customer.

222
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:50,980
Does he live around here?

223
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:53,650
He said he's staying nearby.

224
00:14:55,710 --> 00:14:57,730
[Calls]

225
00:14:57,760 --> 00:15:00,290
[Boss]

226
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:10,950
Mr. Sarm!

227
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:15,440
Mr. Sarm!

228
00:15:16,250 --> 00:15:17,380
Mr. Sarm!

229
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,640
Where are you, Mr. Sarm?!

230
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:38,220
What are you doing over there,

231
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:39,010
Mr. Sarm?

232
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:41,950
Yes.

233
00:15:42,490 --> 00:15:43,530
It's me.

234
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:58,420
I was in search of your boiled crabs.

235
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,760
You think this is funny?

236
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:10,550
Aw.

237
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:11,910
Aw, aw, aww...

238
00:16:12,950 --> 00:16:13,950
Little Jam.

239
00:16:18,050 --> 00:16:19,330
I'm right here.

240
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:21,150
I wasn't gone or anything.

241
00:16:22,830 --> 00:16:24,430
Do not disappear on me again.

242
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:27,350
Do not act crazy like this,

243
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,710
and do not get yourself hurt.

244
00:16:37,050 --> 00:16:38,840
Always telling me what I can and can't do.

245
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:40,440
Who do you think you are?

246
00:16:43,450 --> 00:16:44,450
Do I have to listen to you?

247
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:52,930
Whatever.

248
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:55,140
No means no.

249
00:16:58,640 --> 00:16:59,430
Okay...

250
00:17:00,330 --> 00:17:01,140
"I won't."

251
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:03,530
I won't disappear on you.

252
00:17:04,599 --> 00:17:06,010
I won't act crazy like this,

253
00:17:07,510 --> 00:17:08,599
and I won't get myself hurt.

254
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:12,550
Okay?

255
00:17:15,250 --> 00:17:16,839
Now, stop being a crybaby.

256
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:22,230
Hey...

257
00:19:22,650 --> 00:19:23,430
Snoop.

258
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:27,130
I already told you my name is not Snoop.

259
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:27,830
Oh, did you?

260
00:19:27,870 --> 00:19:29,480
Okay, if that's the case,

261
00:19:30,030 --> 00:19:31,240
mm...

262
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:32,140
Snug.

263
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:33,380
I'll call you Snug, then.

264
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:37,250
Hey.

265
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:40,120
You're really that worried
I'll disappear on you,

266
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:41,140
huh?

267
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:46,540
It is because someone is hunting you down.

268
00:19:47,350 --> 00:19:48,640
If you disappear on me,

269
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:50,430
where am I supposed to find you?

270
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:53,160
And...

271
00:19:56,540 --> 00:19:58,040
how did you get to Ko Pha-ngan?

272
00:19:58,750 --> 00:20:00,950
Why could I not find
any travel information at all?

273
00:20:03,430 --> 00:20:04,220
Well,

274
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:06,530
that's a "secret."

275
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:10,620
What about you?

276
00:20:10,930 --> 00:20:12,280
How did you find me?

277
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:14,320
Same answer.

278
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:16,090
It is a "secret."

279
00:20:17,190 --> 00:20:18,190
Oh...

280
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:20,520
- Always got to have the last word, huh?
- Ouch!

281
00:20:20,560 --> 00:20:21,520
That hurt.

282
00:20:22,630 --> 00:20:23,370
Hey.

283
00:20:24,310 --> 00:20:26,230
Are you planning on following me forever?

284
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:28,140
Not exactly.

285
00:20:28,740 --> 00:20:31,060
Mr. Sib has already set the deadline:

286
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:33,910
Ms. Namnueng's wedding day.

287
00:20:33,950 --> 00:20:35,330
That is only a little over a week away.

288
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:39,400
You are not really returning?

289
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:42,300
Your own sister
is getting married, you know.

290
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:47,340
They can have
their wedding just fine without me.

291
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:50,430
But...

292
00:20:50,530 --> 00:20:53,340
she wants you there on her special day.

293
00:21:16,150 --> 00:21:17,950
You are really not going home?

294
00:21:23,550 --> 00:21:24,750
Perhaps...

295
00:21:27,230 --> 00:21:29,130
you are not ready to meet Mr. PiMai.

296
00:21:38,390 --> 00:21:40,310
I'm just not ready to get scolded by my dad.

297
00:21:46,050 --> 00:21:48,590
This sucks!

298
00:22:32,540 --> 00:22:33,450
Hey!

299
00:22:34,630 --> 00:22:35,430
Hey...

300
00:22:36,350 --> 00:22:37,400
Hey...

301
00:23:18,060 --> 00:23:18,850
Good evening,

302
00:23:19,240 --> 00:23:20,240
Mr. Sarm.

303
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:31,240
Feeling a bit thirsty.

304
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:40,640
You guys really went through
a lot of trouble, huh?

305
00:23:41,570 --> 00:23:42,520
What the hell do you want?

306
00:23:43,030 --> 00:23:44,570
You're quick to catch on.

307
00:23:44,790 --> 00:23:46,160
Get on the boat with us.
Don't make a fuss.

308
00:23:46,330 --> 00:23:46,940
Sure.

309
00:23:47,550 --> 00:23:48,440
But not tonight.

310
00:23:49,010 --> 00:23:50,010
It's getting late.

311
00:23:50,250 --> 00:23:51,040
Go to bed already.

312
00:23:51,470 --> 00:23:52,710
Go home to your wife and kids.

313
00:23:52,750 --> 00:23:53,840
They're probably missing you.

314
00:23:54,260 --> 00:23:55,770
Also, stop trespassing already.

315
00:23:56,940 --> 00:23:58,040
Next time, I'll call the police.

316
00:23:58,070 --> 00:23:59,320
Hey!

317
00:23:59,740 --> 00:24:01,000
Do you want to do this the easy way,

318
00:24:01,360 --> 00:24:02,660
or the hard way?

319
00:24:10,140 --> 00:24:11,230
Fine.

320
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:14,520
If you want me that badly,

321
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:16,150
fine.

322
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:19,840
Get a palanquin and take me away.

323
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:22,710
Get me a yogurt drink, too.

324
00:24:29,610 --> 00:24:30,520
No straw?

325
00:24:30,830 --> 00:24:31,800
Are you nuts?!

326
00:24:31,830 --> 00:24:32,750
Take him!

327
00:24:34,540 --> 00:24:35,120
Hey, hey, hey!

328
00:24:35,250 --> 00:24:36,060
You guys are serious?!

329
00:24:36,350 --> 00:24:37,350
Hey!

330
00:24:40,140 --> 00:24:41,840
You are not taking Mr. Sarm anywhere!

331
00:24:43,780 --> 00:24:45,550
Who sent you here?

332
00:24:46,350 --> 00:24:47,930
If you want something, just ask nicely

333
00:24:48,030 --> 00:24:49,750
instead of breaking in at this hour.

334
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:52,330
I've been searching for him for half a year,

335
00:24:53,350 --> 00:24:54,940
but I couldn't find even a trace of him.

336
00:24:59,040 --> 00:25:00,650
But after you came here,

337
00:25:02,260 --> 00:25:03,720
everything got way easier.

338
00:25:03,750 --> 00:25:04,440
Hey, hey.

339
00:25:04,470 --> 00:25:05,790
- Hey, stop it.
- Be still.

340
00:25:05,820 --> 00:25:06,860
Don't touch him.

341
00:25:07,040 --> 00:25:08,040
It's okay.

342
00:25:14,600 --> 00:25:15,700
That was nothing!

343
00:25:17,110 --> 00:25:18,030
Jam!

344
00:25:19,740 --> 00:25:20,940
This brat!

345
00:25:21,020 --> 00:25:21,630
You.

346
00:25:21,660 --> 00:25:23,320
Let's make you suffer with him, too!

347
00:25:23,350 --> 00:25:24,250
Take them away!

348
00:25:24,430 --> 00:25:26,120
- Hey! Stop!
- Hey, hey, hey!

349
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:27,160
- Be gentle.
- Hey!

350
00:25:27,190 --> 00:25:28,050
- Don't hurt Jam!
- Let me go!

351
00:25:28,090 --> 00:25:28,920
- Stop!
- Jam!

352
00:25:29,340 --> 00:25:30,820
Let go of me!

353
00:25:32,530 --> 00:25:33,130
Hey.

354
00:25:33,300 --> 00:25:34,300
Let's be real here.

355
00:25:34,610 --> 00:25:35,990
Is this a boat or a piece of junk?

356
00:25:36,360 --> 00:25:37,720
Are we even going to make it

357
00:25:37,880 --> 00:25:39,100
to your destination, huh?

358
00:25:39,240 --> 00:25:40,820
I bet it'll sink before we even get there.

359
00:25:41,150 --> 00:25:42,750
We probably won't even make it.

360
00:25:42,840 --> 00:25:45,140
- Pray you make it through the night
- Whoa...

361
00:25:45,300 --> 00:25:46,300
before talking smack.

362
00:25:46,330 --> 00:25:47,330
Wow...

363
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:48,940
What the hell did I ever do to you?

364
00:25:48,980 --> 00:25:50,000
Did I step on your toes or something?

365
00:25:50,040 --> 00:25:51,040
No.

366
00:25:51,070 --> 00:25:52,350
You didn't do anything to us.

367
00:25:53,140 --> 00:25:53,890
But to someone else?

368
00:25:53,920 --> 00:25:54,520
I'm not so sure.

369
00:25:54,570 --> 00:25:55,440
Oh...

370
00:25:56,550 --> 00:25:58,550
Then at least do us a favor
and give us a few hints.

371
00:25:59,340 --> 00:26:00,630
Who hired you?

372
00:26:02,150 --> 00:26:03,440
You know exactly what you did

373
00:26:03,480 --> 00:26:05,150
and to whom.

374
00:26:07,810 --> 00:26:09,450
Why the hell did you stop the boat, though?

375
00:26:09,500 --> 00:26:10,540
What, are we fishing?

376
00:26:10,920 --> 00:26:11,620
Oh, what,

377
00:26:11,660 --> 00:26:12,750
are you putting on a concert now?

378
00:26:13,150 --> 00:26:13,700
Alright.

379
00:26:13,730 --> 00:26:15,690
Raise your right hand!

380
00:26:15,800 --> 00:26:17,920
♫Devote himself to his master♫

381
00:26:18,040 --> 00:26:18,810
♫Shoot...♫

382
00:26:18,850 --> 00:26:19,930
Shut your mouth.

383
00:26:21,650 --> 00:26:22,320
Keep an eye on them.

384
00:26:22,350 --> 00:26:23,350
I need to talk to the boss.

385
00:26:23,760 --> 00:26:24,470
Understood.

386
00:26:24,500 --> 00:26:25,540
Be sure to look at me.

387
00:26:26,140 --> 00:26:27,140
Am I handsome?

388
00:26:27,630 --> 00:26:28,940
Wow, wow.

389
00:26:30,090 --> 00:26:30,820
Huh?

390
00:26:34,760 --> 00:26:35,610
Jam...

391
00:26:35,950 --> 00:26:36,950
Are you okay?

392
00:26:37,650 --> 00:26:38,560
Feeling seasick?

393
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:40,080
Are you?

394
00:26:41,040 --> 00:26:43,080
I am just a little dizzy.

395
00:26:44,170 --> 00:26:45,260
Come closer, then.

396
00:26:58,330 --> 00:26:59,650
You are in trouble.

397
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:01,860
They are going to hurt you.

398
00:27:02,650 --> 00:27:03,550
Don't worry.

399
00:27:03,870 --> 00:27:05,500
No one can touch me.

400
00:27:05,540 --> 00:27:06,540
I'm...

401
00:27:06,940 --> 00:27:08,320
a tiger with nine lives.

402
00:27:09,340 --> 00:27:11,600
It is "a cat with nine lives."

403
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:14,660
I really do not understand you.

404
00:27:14,990 --> 00:27:17,450
Why do you always
take everything so lightly?

405
00:27:18,760 --> 00:27:20,250
I'm not, Jam.

406
00:27:20,580 --> 00:27:21,640
Look at me.

407
00:27:22,430 --> 00:27:23,530
I'm serious.

408
00:27:23,830 --> 00:27:24,830
I mean it.

409
00:27:27,740 --> 00:27:29,360
Do not get hurt, okay?

410
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:31,710
That is not allowed.

411
00:27:32,110 --> 00:27:33,080
I know.

412
00:27:34,570 --> 00:27:35,900
My dad's feng shui master

413
00:27:36,100 --> 00:27:36,940
told me

414
00:27:37,100 --> 00:27:38,340
I'd live for over a hundred years,

415
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:40,240
so don't worry.

416
00:27:40,550 --> 00:27:41,440
I don't die easily.

417
00:27:41,550 --> 00:27:42,660
Do not jinx it.

418
00:27:42,690 --> 00:27:43,320
What?

419
00:27:43,350 --> 00:27:44,960
How dare you say that?

420
00:27:46,630 --> 00:27:47,330
Come on.

421
00:27:47,460 --> 00:27:48,340
Just believe me.

422
00:27:48,670 --> 00:27:49,130
Hey!

423
00:27:50,830 --> 00:27:51,680
What's up?

424
00:27:51,810 --> 00:27:52,620
You two...

425
00:27:54,350 --> 00:27:55,420
It's time.

426
00:27:55,870 --> 00:27:56,660
Is it?

427
00:27:56,700 --> 00:27:58,390
What should we do with this kid?

428
00:27:58,420 --> 00:27:59,240
Hey, hey.

429
00:27:59,390 --> 00:28:00,640
Don't do anything to this kid.

430
00:28:01,250 --> 00:28:02,440
A word of advice:

431
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:03,230
this is...

432
00:28:03,570 --> 00:28:04,530
one of Sattawat's men.

433
00:28:05,460 --> 00:28:06,930
If anything happens to him,

434
00:28:07,140 --> 00:28:08,750
Sattawat won't let any of you live.

435
00:28:09,360 --> 00:28:10,970
If he doesn't report back to Sattawat

436
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:13,380
within 24 hours,

437
00:28:13,540 --> 00:28:15,250
Sattawat will surely
scour the earth to find him!

438
00:28:15,880 --> 00:28:16,930
So let him go.

439
00:28:16,980 --> 00:28:17,790
Take me instead.

440
00:28:17,820 --> 00:28:18,820
Do whatever you want with me!

441
00:28:18,860 --> 00:28:19,490
Throw me into a pot.

442
00:28:19,520 --> 00:28:20,100
Turn me into a pizza

443
00:28:20,130 --> 00:28:21,050
or tteokbokki.

444
00:28:21,180 --> 00:28:22,210
Just let this kid go.

445
00:28:22,710 --> 00:28:23,390
Right.

446
00:28:23,620 --> 00:28:24,780
Stick to the original plan.

447
00:28:25,320 --> 00:28:25,820
Yes.

448
00:28:25,930 --> 00:28:26,930
Don't worry, Jam.

449
00:28:27,220 --> 00:28:28,080
Go first.

450
00:28:28,110 --> 00:28:29,010
You have to survive, okay?

451
00:28:29,050 --> 00:28:29,900
No!

452
00:28:29,940 --> 00:28:30,720
- Don't worry about me.
- Let go of him.

453
00:28:30,810 --> 00:28:31,810
This tiger has nine lives.

454
00:28:31,920 --> 00:28:33,450
- Hey!
- I'll be with you soon.

455
00:28:33,770 --> 00:28:34,510
- I'll be right behind you.
- Hey!

456
00:28:34,550 --> 00:28:35,210
Hey, be gentle!

457
00:28:35,260 --> 00:28:36,410
- The kid's this tiny!
- Hey!

458
00:28:36,710 --> 00:28:37,640
Hey!

459
00:28:40,530 --> 00:28:40,960
Hey!!

460
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:42,000
What the hell did you do?!

461
00:28:42,100 --> 00:28:42,890
Let go of me!

462
00:28:43,210 --> 00:28:44,050
Let me go!

463
00:28:44,140 --> 00:28:45,320
You're all dead!

464
00:28:45,420 --> 00:28:46,910
Sattawat will come for your throat!

465
00:28:46,970 --> 00:28:48,120
And so will I!

466
00:28:50,410 --> 00:28:51,110
Jam...

467
00:28:54,710 --> 00:28:56,620
Thee, any news?

468
00:28:57,720 --> 00:28:58,720
No, Uncle.

469
00:28:59,710 --> 00:29:00,620
Honestly,

470
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:02,410
I really feel for you, Thee.

471
00:29:02,580 --> 00:29:04,210
You have to work so much harder.

472
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:05,930
Sarm, oh, Sarm.

473
00:29:06,270 --> 00:29:07,320
He's a grown man,

474
00:29:07,710 --> 00:29:09,120
but he's still acting so irresponsibly.

475
00:29:10,310 --> 00:29:11,440
It's not that bad, Song.

476
00:29:12,010 --> 00:29:13,690
No matter how complicated...

477
00:29:13,730 --> 00:29:14,560
the workload

478
00:29:14,600 --> 00:29:16,700
Sarm left behind was,

479
00:29:16,930 --> 00:29:18,810
I handled it with ease.

480
00:29:19,290 --> 00:29:20,630
It's the opposite, actually.

481
00:29:21,240 --> 00:29:23,310
I'm actually honored

482
00:29:23,810 --> 00:29:24,910
to take care of the empire

483
00:29:24,950 --> 00:29:27,910
you built with
your own blood, sweat, and tears.

484
00:29:28,670 --> 00:29:30,610
But Sarm...

485
00:29:30,700 --> 00:29:33,010
ended up neglecting it so badly.

486
00:29:34,150 --> 00:29:36,020
He's made himself this clear.

487
00:29:36,890 --> 00:29:39,280
Why not consider Thee, Dad?

488
00:29:42,700 --> 00:29:44,110
What are you talking about, Sib?

489
00:29:48,210 --> 00:29:49,210
That said,

490
00:29:49,520 --> 00:29:51,600
what if Sarm actually...

491
00:29:51,810 --> 00:29:53,620
can't handle the work when he comes back?

492
00:29:55,610 --> 00:29:56,910
The word "can't"

493
00:29:57,920 --> 00:29:59,520
isn't in Sarm's dictionary, Song.

494
00:30:00,060 --> 00:30:01,130
There's only...

495
00:30:01,620 --> 00:30:02,620
"I want to do it"

496
00:30:02,660 --> 00:30:03,990
or "I don't want to do it."

497
00:30:04,630 --> 00:30:06,340
Come to think of it, you're right.

498
00:30:06,430 --> 00:30:07,200
Right now,

499
00:30:07,350 --> 00:30:08,430
Sarm is probably off...

500
00:30:08,720 --> 00:30:10,920
being his quirky self somewhere.

501
00:30:12,720 --> 00:30:13,920
Either that, or...

502
00:30:14,630 --> 00:30:17,630
Sarm's probably
falling in love with Ko Pha-ngan.

503
00:30:23,010 --> 00:30:24,770
I have found Mr. Sarm.

504
00:30:24,800 --> 00:30:25,880
On Ko Pha-ngan.

505
00:30:29,310 --> 00:30:30,310
It's too bad, really.

506
00:30:50,240 --> 00:30:51,520
Jam!

507
00:30:51,730 --> 00:30:52,910
Little Jam!

508
00:30:53,300 --> 00:30:54,440
Jam!!

509
00:30:55,910 --> 00:30:56,910
Jam!

510
00:30:56,950 --> 00:30:57,950
Jam...

511
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:00,400
Jam!

512
00:31:00,900 --> 00:31:02,100
Jam...

513
00:31:02,320 --> 00:31:03,320
Jam!!

514
00:31:03,830 --> 00:31:04,590
Jam!

515
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:07,200
Mr. Sarm...

516
00:31:08,600 --> 00:31:09,300
Yeah.

517
00:31:10,010 --> 00:31:10,820
That's right...

518
00:31:10,940 --> 00:31:12,010
It's me.

519
00:31:13,650 --> 00:31:14,320
A ghost...

520
00:31:14,350 --> 00:31:15,770
What are you talking about?
I'm still alive!

521
00:31:16,810 --> 00:31:17,810
Are you hurt?

522
00:31:20,910 --> 00:31:21,910
Little Jam...

523
00:31:26,680 --> 00:31:27,680
You got stung by a sea urchin.

524
00:31:28,410 --> 00:31:30,320
You find a way to get yourself hurt
every single day.

525
00:31:30,700 --> 00:31:32,310
How did you end up here?

526
00:31:33,900 --> 00:31:35,300
I zoomed over here in a long-tail boat.

527
00:31:37,210 --> 00:31:37,910
Little Jam.

528
00:31:37,950 --> 00:31:39,150
What about...

529
00:31:39,290 --> 00:31:40,910
those guys?

530
00:31:42,110 --> 00:31:43,110
It's a long story.

531
00:31:43,810 --> 00:31:44,930
Worry about yourself first.

532
00:31:52,110 --> 00:31:53,030
Ready?

533
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:56,490
Is it going to hurt?

534
00:31:56,680 --> 00:31:58,170
Like your heart's about to burst.

535
00:31:59,520 --> 00:32:01,010
Is it that painful?

536
00:32:01,200 --> 00:32:02,160
Mm.

537
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:06,450
Ready?

538
00:32:10,410 --> 00:32:11,720
If it hurts, pinch my leg.

539
00:32:13,220 --> 00:32:14,600
Mm...

540
00:32:15,230 --> 00:32:16,010
All good?

541
00:32:16,170 --> 00:32:16,830
Ready?

542
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:17,660
Mm.

543
00:32:24,320 --> 00:32:25,110
Three...

544
00:32:25,530 --> 00:32:26,290
Two...

545
00:32:30,420 --> 00:32:31,130
Done.

546
00:32:35,220 --> 00:32:36,000
See?

547
00:32:36,290 --> 00:32:37,290
It didn't hurt at all.

548
00:32:42,290 --> 00:32:42,910
Here.

549
00:32:45,320 --> 00:32:46,130
Get up.

550
00:32:48,020 --> 00:32:49,200
Come on. Get up already.

551
00:32:49,350 --> 00:32:51,080
We can do this the easy way or the hard way.

552
00:32:52,520 --> 00:32:54,300
Can you get a little lower?

553
00:32:54,410 --> 00:32:55,730
I cannot get up...

554
00:32:57,620 --> 00:32:58,630
So extra.

555
00:32:59,710 --> 00:33:00,800
Such a pain.

556
00:33:01,510 --> 00:33:02,510
Come on. Hop on.

557
00:33:11,290 --> 00:33:12,290
Hold on tight, okay?

558
00:33:13,310 --> 00:33:14,600
Or you'll fall again.

559
00:33:15,110 --> 00:33:15,940
Are we good to go?

560
00:33:16,810 --> 00:33:17,810
Thank you...

561
00:33:19,040 --> 00:33:19,930
Thank who?

562
00:33:20,220 --> 00:33:20,820
Huh?

563
00:33:20,950 --> 00:33:21,900
The forest spirits?

564
00:33:21,930 --> 00:33:22,800
Water spirit?

565
00:33:22,910 --> 00:33:23,910
Or who?

566
00:33:25,220 --> 00:33:26,890
Thank you, Mr. Sarm.

567
00:33:27,220 --> 00:33:28,220
Didn't catch that.

568
00:33:28,730 --> 00:33:29,730
Who were you thanking?

569
00:33:30,910 --> 00:33:33,180
I said, "Thank you, Mr. Sarm!"

570
00:33:33,210 --> 00:33:34,000
Yeah!

571
00:33:34,170 --> 00:33:35,230
That's more like it.

572
00:33:35,620 --> 00:33:36,500
Say it loud and clear

573
00:33:36,530 --> 00:33:38,720
just like when you were
shouting at me back there.

574
00:33:39,910 --> 00:33:40,820
Let's go.

575
00:33:40,970 --> 00:33:41,970
Hold on tight, alright?

576
00:33:52,850 --> 00:33:53,980
You are fated to suffer

577
00:33:54,010 --> 00:33:55,250
the same misfortune as your parents.

578
00:33:56,970 --> 00:33:57,810
Jam!

579
00:33:58,050 --> 00:33:59,050
Hey!

580
00:34:20,210 --> 00:34:21,429
Still being stubborn?

581
00:34:22,790 --> 00:34:23,909
You're too weak right now.

582
00:34:24,120 --> 00:34:25,120
Where do you think you're going?

583
00:34:26,780 --> 00:34:28,280
You might fall into the ocean again.

584
00:34:28,710 --> 00:34:30,330
This time,
no one will be there to save you.

585
00:34:30,949 --> 00:34:32,500
You are being so dramatic.

586
00:34:36,620 --> 00:34:38,010
Where are we, anyway?

587
00:34:38,670 --> 00:34:39,310
Well...

588
00:34:39,710 --> 00:34:41,380
we're on some beach on Ko Samui.

589
00:34:41,710 --> 00:34:43,320
- Ko Samui?
- Mm.

590
00:34:45,010 --> 00:34:46,310
And whose house is this?

591
00:34:46,909 --> 00:34:48,199
You're pretty observant.

592
00:34:49,210 --> 00:34:49,900
Well...

593
00:34:50,080 --> 00:34:51,400
I was too lazy to go into town,

594
00:34:51,530 --> 00:34:53,199
so I asked some locals
if I could stay here for the night.

595
00:34:53,909 --> 00:34:55,360
This is the place they gave me.

596
00:34:57,100 --> 00:34:58,590
Oh...

597
00:35:00,730 --> 00:35:01,520
Mm.

598
00:35:01,780 --> 00:35:02,610
Are you hungry?

599
00:35:07,010 --> 00:35:07,850
Mm.

600
00:35:09,650 --> 00:35:10,700
Come.

601
00:35:14,050 --> 00:35:14,720
Come on.

602
00:35:18,100 --> 00:35:19,100
You can hold my hand.

603
00:35:19,790 --> 00:35:20,790
I won't charge you.

604
00:35:24,130 --> 00:35:24,910
Mm.

605
00:35:27,930 --> 00:35:28,720
Come.

606
00:35:31,190 --> 00:35:31,910
Ow!

607
00:35:41,430 --> 00:35:42,470
Help her out.

608
00:35:43,030 --> 00:35:44,170
Auntie, let me help you.

609
00:35:44,210 --> 00:35:45,580
It's okay, dear.

610
00:35:49,830 --> 00:35:50,520
How are you?

611
00:35:50,560 --> 00:35:51,110
Thank you.

612
00:35:51,140 --> 00:35:52,080
Feeling better?

613
00:35:52,210 --> 00:35:53,730
A whole lot better now.

614
00:35:54,240 --> 00:35:55,360
Has your fever gone down?

615
00:35:56,690 --> 00:35:58,080
Thank you.

616
00:35:58,110 --> 00:35:59,110
Eat up, dear.

617
00:36:01,530 --> 00:36:03,020
I'm back!

618
00:36:04,130 --> 00:36:04,930
- He's drunk...
- Oh!

619
00:36:05,400 --> 00:36:06,270
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

620
00:36:06,310 --> 00:36:07,310
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

621
00:36:08,720 --> 00:36:09,720
- Good evening.
- Right.

622
00:36:09,750 --> 00:36:11,080
- Now, now.
- Good evening.

623
00:36:11,120 --> 00:36:12,000
Let's have dinner

624
00:36:12,030 --> 00:36:13,400
so you can take your pills.

625
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:14,920
How are you feeling?

626
00:36:15,320 --> 00:36:17,330
Little one, has your fever gone down?

627
00:36:17,450 --> 00:36:18,840
A whole lot better now, Uncle.

628
00:36:19,900 --> 00:36:21,220
If you're not better,

629
00:36:21,330 --> 00:36:22,830
come enjoy a drink with me.

630
00:36:22,990 --> 00:36:24,040
A sip or two

631
00:36:24,080 --> 00:36:25,080
will surely make it go away!

632
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:26,710
- Now, now.
- Alright.

633
00:36:26,750 --> 00:36:28,260
- Let's have dinner.
- Alright, alright.

634
00:36:28,700 --> 00:36:31,080
You always
invite everyone you meet to drink.

635
00:36:31,120 --> 00:36:32,880
- Let's have dinner.
- Right, right, right.

636
00:36:32,910 --> 00:36:34,620
- Let us eat.
- Right?

637
00:36:45,510 --> 00:36:47,100
Whoa...

638
00:36:47,140 --> 00:36:48,140
Here.

639
00:36:48,170 --> 00:36:49,520
- Sweet, right?
- Let me show you how it's done.

640
00:36:50,430 --> 00:36:50,980
Eyes on me.

641
00:36:51,020 --> 00:36:52,710
Watch and learn.

642
00:36:52,860 --> 00:36:53,760
Like this.

643
00:36:53,790 --> 00:36:55,470
Gently pry it upward.

644
00:36:55,500 --> 00:36:56,630
Don't touch the bones.

645
00:36:58,340 --> 00:36:59,290
Alright. Dig in.

646
00:36:59,320 --> 00:37:00,110
Try it.

647
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:01,840
Go on.

648
00:37:04,240 --> 00:37:05,710
It was hot.

649
00:37:06,070 --> 00:37:07,820
I did not notice the bones.

650
00:37:08,290 --> 00:37:09,290
Hey...

651
00:37:10,310 --> 00:37:13,050
A true warrior is bound to have a few scars.

652
00:37:16,020 --> 00:37:17,520
You have to watch out for the bones, too.

653
00:37:17,550 --> 00:37:18,810
What if you choke on them?

654
00:37:18,920 --> 00:37:19,710
What?

655
00:37:20,520 --> 00:37:22,700
This is how I eat, alright?

656
00:37:25,230 --> 00:37:26,310
Does "Jiranat" mean

657
00:37:26,770 --> 00:37:27,770
"burden" or something?

658
00:37:27,820 --> 00:37:28,620
Hm?

659
00:37:29,100 --> 00:37:30,100
And does "Traiphop"

660
00:37:30,330 --> 00:37:32,530
mean "snarky"?

661
00:37:33,930 --> 00:37:36,650
I never wanted to be a burden to you.

662
00:37:37,220 --> 00:37:39,800
Young man,
what made you so foul-mouthed?

663
00:37:40,920 --> 00:37:42,520
Jam, don't mind him.

664
00:37:42,550 --> 00:37:43,690
As the old saying goes,

665
00:37:43,720 --> 00:37:44,970
"The more a dog barks,

666
00:37:45,010 --> 00:37:46,490
the more it loves its owner."

667
00:37:52,720 --> 00:37:53,720
Try it. It's tasty.

668
00:37:55,230 --> 00:37:56,480
Try the fish with this.

669
00:38:04,630 --> 00:38:06,520
Since last night...

670
00:38:06,650 --> 00:38:09,040
Mr. Sarm has been acting strange.

671
00:38:09,480 --> 00:38:11,320
He still talks the same as always,

672
00:38:11,500 --> 00:38:13,100
but his eyes...

673
00:38:13,550 --> 00:38:15,710
somehow look sadder.

674
00:38:21,030 --> 00:38:21,630
Oh.

675
00:38:21,850 --> 00:38:22,510
It's late.

676
00:38:22,810 --> 00:38:23,920
Why are you still up?

677
00:38:26,810 --> 00:38:28,210
I am waiting for you...

678
00:38:28,990 --> 00:38:29,910
Oh...

679
00:38:30,020 --> 00:38:31,020
Oh...

680
00:38:33,130 --> 00:38:34,810
I mean, I have been waiting for you
to get in here

681
00:38:35,120 --> 00:38:36,220
so I can close the mosquito net.

682
00:38:37,320 --> 00:38:38,120
You're right.

683
00:38:43,870 --> 00:38:45,410
Can we sleep with the lights on?

684
00:38:50,690 --> 00:38:51,530
Oh...

685
00:38:53,100 --> 00:38:54,530
It's so bright...

686
00:38:56,610 --> 00:38:58,010
You might get a migraine.

687
00:38:59,320 --> 00:39:00,600
We don't have any medicine either.

688
00:39:03,960 --> 00:39:05,020
I understand.

689
00:39:05,710 --> 00:39:06,710
We can turn them off, then.

690
00:39:30,600 --> 00:39:31,810
Mr. Sarm.

691
00:39:33,330 --> 00:39:34,120
What?

692
00:39:36,560 --> 00:39:37,720
You seem stressed.

693
00:39:41,810 --> 00:39:42,810
Based on what?

694
00:39:44,720 --> 00:39:45,400
Well...

695
00:39:45,770 --> 00:39:47,820
you were frowning the whole time.

696
00:39:47,850 --> 00:39:48,790
Oh.

697
00:39:49,630 --> 00:39:50,300
Hey,

698
00:39:50,610 --> 00:39:51,610
did you know that

699
00:39:52,020 --> 00:39:53,170
a man who frowns

700
00:39:53,190 --> 00:39:54,220
like this

701
00:39:55,190 --> 00:39:56,250
looks badass?

702
00:39:56,550 --> 00:39:58,320
Like... it makes him look cool.

703
00:39:58,450 --> 00:39:59,510
Cool, you know?

704
00:40:04,300 --> 00:40:05,300
Not true.

705
00:40:08,910 --> 00:40:10,320
You are being evasive.

706
00:40:11,820 --> 00:40:12,600
Hey.

707
00:40:13,040 --> 00:40:14,140
What are you fussing about?

708
00:40:14,360 --> 00:40:16,030
Hm? Tell me.

709
00:40:21,120 --> 00:40:22,320
You are the one acting strange.

710
00:40:22,480 --> 00:40:23,410
What has gotten into you?

711
00:40:23,620 --> 00:40:24,620
Why will you not tell me?

712
00:40:30,630 --> 00:40:31,390
If I told you,

713
00:40:31,430 --> 00:40:32,710
you'd think I was cringe.

714
00:40:32,800 --> 00:40:34,030
You already are.

715
00:40:40,960 --> 00:40:41,640
Let's sleep.

716
00:40:41,670 --> 00:40:42,560
I refuse.

717
00:40:42,590 --> 00:40:43,300
Sleep. Now.

718
00:40:43,330 --> 00:40:44,000
No.

719
00:40:44,040 --> 00:40:45,210
I told you, it's nothing.

720
00:40:45,250 --> 00:40:45,960
You are lying.

721
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:46,440
Sleep!

722
00:40:46,470 --> 00:40:47,180
I refuse.

723
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:49,800
Okay.

724
00:40:51,630 --> 00:40:53,490
You need me to lull you to sleep first,

725
00:40:53,520 --> 00:40:54,410
don't you?

726
00:40:54,450 --> 00:40:55,390
Fine.

727
00:40:55,630 --> 00:40:56,460
Want me to sing, too?

728
00:40:56,620 --> 00:40:57,620
Want me to pat your bum, too?

729
00:40:58,010 --> 00:40:59,490
Hush now.

730
00:40:59,610 --> 00:41:00,610
Sleep tight.

731
00:41:00,650 --> 00:41:01,360
Go to sleep.

732
00:41:01,390 --> 00:41:02,310
Stop it.

733
00:41:03,220 --> 00:41:04,100
Why?

734
00:41:04,420 --> 00:41:05,280
This will make you sleep.

735
00:41:05,310 --> 00:41:06,670
Go to sleep. Hush now.

736
00:41:06,710 --> 00:41:08,020
Enough already.

737
00:42:25,420 --> 00:42:26,600
Damn it!

738
00:42:26,800 --> 00:42:28,610
The kitten is being needy!

739
00:43:43,450 --> 00:43:44,300
How is it?

740
00:43:44,640 --> 00:43:45,580
Can you see clearly now?

741
00:43:45,690 --> 00:43:46,430
Mm.

742
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:48,100
What's this?

743
00:43:51,230 --> 00:43:52,850
Fat...

744
00:43:52,920 --> 00:43:53,720
fingers.

745
00:43:56,950 --> 00:43:58,000
And what about this?

746
00:44:02,250 --> 00:44:03,250
A heart.

747
00:44:05,010 --> 00:44:06,010
It's actually my own heart.

748
00:44:10,630 --> 00:44:12,520
Did you have trouble sleeping last night?

749
00:44:14,610 --> 00:44:18,720
♫I only wish you nothing but the best♫

750
00:44:18,750 --> 00:44:23,130
♫Hoping your smile will never fade♫

751
00:44:23,210 --> 00:44:27,840
♫I'll stay right here by your side♫

752
00:44:32,750 --> 00:44:34,240
Do you want to get a haircut?

753
00:44:34,280 --> 00:44:35,010
Hey...

754
00:44:35,530 --> 00:44:37,290
What doesn't your backpack have? Hm?

755
00:44:37,570 --> 00:44:38,790
It contains everything

756
00:44:39,120 --> 00:44:40,050
based on the concept:

757
00:44:40,070 --> 00:44:42,370
"My backpack has things
that others do not have."

758
00:44:42,400 --> 00:44:44,420
Can you give me a haircut, then?

759
00:44:45,050 --> 00:44:46,450
This house has no mirrors.

760
00:44:46,890 --> 00:44:47,980
Let me help you with that.

761
00:44:48,100 --> 00:44:49,100
I can trust you, right?

762
00:44:49,410 --> 00:44:51,400
Be sure to stay still, then.

763
00:44:51,650 --> 00:44:52,410
Alright.

764
00:44:52,550 --> 00:44:53,500
Make me look handsome.

765
00:44:55,730 --> 00:44:57,090
But it's hard to get
any more handsome than this.

766
00:45:01,310 --> 00:45:03,210
Oh... It's a powerful one, too?

767
00:45:05,910 --> 00:45:07,410
All done.

768
00:45:11,710 --> 00:45:12,510
How do I look?

769
00:45:14,060 --> 00:45:15,510
Do I look handsome enough now?

770
00:45:16,110 --> 00:45:17,490
No, no, no.

771
00:45:17,740 --> 00:45:19,060
Don't let your heart melt just yet,

772
00:45:19,130 --> 00:45:20,020
for this...

773
00:45:20,320 --> 00:45:21,230
is only the beginning.

774
00:45:28,840 --> 00:45:30,640
I'm going squid fishing with Uncle Keua.

775
00:45:31,520 --> 00:45:32,520
You'll be okay here, right?

776
00:45:34,110 --> 00:45:35,110
Mm...

777
00:45:35,600 --> 00:45:36,900
Why would I not be?

778
00:45:37,590 --> 00:45:38,890
Then I'll only be away physically, okay?

779
00:46:00,360 --> 00:46:02,160
[Mission: Hunt Down the Teeny-tiny Tiger]

780
00:46:02,770 --> 00:46:04,360
I used to think that...

781
00:46:04,400 --> 00:46:07,460
my mission was simply to find Mr. Sarm.

782
00:46:07,490 --> 00:46:08,690
Today...

783
00:46:08,730 --> 00:46:10,550
I finally found him.

784
00:46:10,570 --> 00:46:12,250
What's harder now...

785
00:46:12,290 --> 00:46:13,700
is making him believe that

786
00:46:13,730 --> 00:46:15,970
he no longer has to run away

787
00:46:16,660 --> 00:46:17,710
from his past,

788
00:46:17,740 --> 00:46:18,790
his pain,

789
00:46:18,820 --> 00:46:21,090
or those hunting him down.

790
00:46:21,150 --> 00:46:22,580
From now on...

791
00:46:22,640 --> 00:46:24,850
I shall remain by his side

792
00:46:24,880 --> 00:46:26,620
until he finds the courage...

793
00:46:26,660 --> 00:46:30,020
to face everything once more.

794
00:46:30,200 --> 00:46:32,330
We've been through so much together,

795
00:46:33,480 --> 00:46:35,050
so how about we become friends?

796
00:46:37,780 --> 00:46:38,970
I've decided.

797
00:46:39,180 --> 00:46:40,830
We're going back to Ko Pha-ngan tomorrow.

798
00:46:40,980 --> 00:46:42,270
I think I am going to head back.

799
00:46:42,700 --> 00:46:44,850
I want you to come with me.

800
00:46:47,100 --> 00:46:48,940
Will we get to see each other again?

801
00:46:49,240 --> 00:46:50,500
You'll want to see me again, of course.

802
00:46:50,550 --> 00:46:52,350
And you'll miss me a lot, too.

803
00:46:54,190 --> 00:47:00,380
♫It seems like something's moving♫

804
00:47:00,460 --> 00:47:06,860
♫What's in my heart isn't too much, but I only♫

805
00:47:06,930 --> 00:47:11,080
♫I only wish you nothing but the best♫

806
00:47:11,150 --> 00:47:15,400
♫Hoping your smile will never fade♫

807
00:47:15,580 --> 00:47:20,250
♫That's all, for I don't wish
to take someone's place♫

808
00:47:20,350 --> 00:47:24,550
♫I'll simply be right here, always within reach♫

809
00:47:24,600 --> 00:47:29,050
♫Like a gentle breeze bringing you peace♫

810
00:47:29,110 --> 00:47:35,680
♫I'll stay right here by your side, always♫

811
00:47:42,570 --> 00:47:48,510
♫I'll stay right here by your side♫

812
00:47:49,180 --> 00:47:51,910
[Your Third Series]
